---

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  ogImage?: string;
  type?: "website" | "article";
}

const {
  title,
  description = "Senior software engineer with 12 years across backend, front-end, infrastructure and teams. Founder-engineer in Lisbon who takes products from the first version to production, with AI where it helps. Open to fractional and contract build work. My own products: a second brain for AI agents, and Damasqo, verified bank data.",
  ogImage = "/og-image.png",
  type = "website",
} = Astro.props;

const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site ?? Astro.url).href;
const ogImageURL = new URL(ogImage, Astro.site ?? Astro.url).href;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="author" content="Gil Neto" />
    <meta
      name="keywords"
      content="founder-engineer, AI product engineer, AI engineer Lisbon, agent memory, long-term memory for LLM agents, AI second brain, exocortex, persistent memory architecture, personal knowledge management, context engineering, semantic retrieval, LLM application engineer, fractional build, systems architect, RAG, model evaluation, eval harness, AI agents, document extraction, B2B SaaS, Next.js, TypeScript, Python, Temporal, Lisbon, EU remote, hire"
    />
    <link
      rel="alternate"
      type="application/rss+xml"
      title="Gil Neto — Writing"
      href="/rss.xml"
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico?v=2" sizes="48x48" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg?v=2" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png?v=2" />
    <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest?v=2" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#161f35" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="preload"
      as="style"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&display=swap"
    />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
      media="print"
      onload="this.media='all'"
    />
    <noscript>
      <link
        href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&display=swap"
        rel="stylesheet"
      />
    </noscript>
    <title>{title}</title>

    <!-- Open Graph & Twitter Card -->
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Gil Neto" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content={type} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImageURL} />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImageURL} />

    <!-- JSON-LD: Person + WebSite + FAQ -->
    <script
      type="application/ld+json"
      set:html={JSON.stringify({
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@graph": [
          {
            "@type": "Person",
            "@id": "https://gil-neto.com/#gil",
            name: "Gil Neto",
            url: "https://gil-neto.com",
            jobTitle: "Founder-Engineer & Senior Software Engineer",
            description:
              "Senior engineer with 12 years across backend, front-end, infrastructure and teams, who takes products from the first version to production, with AI where it helps. Works on the rule that the model does judgment and deterministic code does correctness. Builds and runs two products of his own: Damasqo, verified bank data for accountants (Damasqo Capture, former Koa, the deterministic statement-extraction engine; Damasqo Flow, former Kelaro, the accountant's bank-to-spreadsheet sync; Damasqo Hub, former Cashew, a personal finance manager), and a second brain that gives an LLM agent persistent long-term memory.",
            email: "gilneto8.work@gmail.com",
            telephone: "+351914847254",
            address: {
              "@type": "PostalAddress",
              addressLocality: "Lisbon",
              addressCountry: "PT",
            },
            knowsAbout: [
              "Software Architecture",
              "B2B SaaS",
              "Full-Stack Development",
              "Systems Architecture",
              "Infrastructure Engineering",
              "TypeScript",
              "Python",
              "Next.js",
              "React",
              "Node.js",
              "Nest.js",
              "Fastify",
              "Flask",
              "FastAPI",
              "Temporal",
              "PostgreSQL",
              "MongoDB",
              "Redis",
              "BullMQ",
              "Kafka",
              "Docker",
              "Nginx",
              "AWS",
              "GCP",
              "Stripe",
              "OAuth 2.0",
              "Open Banking",
              "PSD2",
              "LLM Integration",
              "LLM Application Architecture",
              "Retrieval-Augmented Generation",
              "pgvector",
              "Model Evaluation",
              "Eval Harnesses",
              "AI Agents",
              "Agent Orchestration",
              "Document Extraction",
              "Deterministic NLP",
              "Agent Memory",
              "Long-Term Memory for LLM Agents",
              "Persistent Memory Architecture",
              "Personal Knowledge Management",
              "Second Brain Systems",
              "Bank Reconciliation",
              "Accounting Automation",
              "Knowledge Base Architecture",
              "Context Engineering",
              "Semantic Retrieval",
            ],
            alumniOf: {
              "@type": "CollegeOrUniversity",
              name: "Faculdade de Ciências e Tecnologia - Universidade Nova de Lisboa",
            },
            seeks: [
              "Fractional and contract build work: architecture, first working version and handover",
              "Bank-data and accounting pipelines",
            ],
            sameAs: [
              "https://github.com/gilneto8",
              "https://www.linkedin.com/in/gil-neto-7b44946a",
              "https://dev.to/gilneto8",
            ],
            workLocation: {
              "@type": "Place",
              name: "Lisbon, Portugal · Remote (EU)",
            },
          },
          {
            "@type": "WebSite",
            "@id": "https://gil-neto.com/#website",
            url: "https://gil-neto.com",
            name: "Gil Neto — Founder-Engineer & Senior Software Engineer",
            description:
              "Portfolio and writing of Gil Neto, a Lisbon-based founder-engineer and senior software engineer who builds products end-to-end: Damasqo (verified bank data) and a second brain for AI agents.",
            inLanguage: "en",
            publisher: { "@id": "https://gil-neto.com/#gil" },
          },
          {
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            mainEntity: [
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "Who is Gil Neto?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Gil Neto is a senior software engineer with 12 years' experience, based in Lisbon, Portugal. He works as a founder-engineer: contract build work for clients across backend, front-end and infrastructure, alongside two products of his own, built and run solo. Damasqo verifies bank data for accountants (Capture extracts and ties out bank statements, Flow syncs client bank accounts into the practice's own spreadsheet, Hub is a personal finance manager), and the second brain gives an LLM agent persistent long-term memory with a scored nightly eval. Both run on one rule: the model does judgment, deterministic code does correctness.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "Does Gil Neto work on AI and LLM products?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Yes. Gil Neto works as a senior software engineer on AI products, building LLM-backed systems where the model handles judgment and deterministic code handles correctness. That covers agent memory and persistent knowledge architecture, LLM application architecture, retrieval-augmented generation, model evaluation and eval harnesses as release gates, agent orchestration, and document extraction. He is open to fractional and contract build work, based in Lisbon and remote across EU timezones.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "What AI systems has Gil Neto built?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Damasqo Capture, former Koa, a deterministic document-extraction engine built as the deliberate alternative to vision-LLM extraction for bank statements: it forces balances to reconcile and refuses loudly rather than returning a plausible total. the pipeline of Damasqo Flow, former Kelaro, running on durable Temporal workflows with the model kept out of the arithmetic. An agentic development pipeline called midas, which resolves every open decision before anything is specified, built on top of Matt Pocock's wayfinder model. A second-brain system giving an LLM agent persistent long-term memory: a markdown knowledge base the agent reads and writes, with capture, routing and checkpointing enforced by lifecycle hooks rather than prompts, retrieval split between generated indexes for state and vector search for specific facts, and a scored nightly eval that detects when the index has gone stale. Earlier, the LLM-integration layer at Opplane between 2021 and 2026.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "What kind of work is Gil Neto open to?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Fractional and contract build work, on whatever the product needs: the architecture, the first working version and the handover. Deepest in bank-data and accounting pipelines, LLM-backed products and agent memory. Remote across EU timezones, based in Lisbon.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "What is Gil Neto's primary tech stack?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "TypeScript, Python, and SQL as primary languages. Next.js, React, Node.js, Nest.js, Fastify, Flask, and Temporal for runtime. Docker, Nginx, PostgreSQL, pgvector, MongoDB, Redis, BullMQ, Kafka on AWS and GCP for infrastructure. Integrations with Stripe, OAuth 2.0, Open Banking (PSD2), Brevo, and Umami.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "What is Gil Neto's technical philosophy?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Memory as infrastructure: an agent that forgets is a demo, so capture, routing and evaluation are enforced by the harness while judgment stays the model's job. Infrastructure-first: own the boundary from DNS to UI, everything containerized and reproducible. AI-augmented execution: leverage coding agents to eliminate boilerplate and focus on architecture and business logic.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "What products has Gil Neto shipped?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Damasqo, verified bank data for accountants: Damasqo Flow, former Kelaro (kelaro.io), in closed beta with one pilot practice in Portugal, and Damasqo Capture, former Koa, the deterministic bank-statement extraction engine behind it, built as the alternative to vision-LLM extraction; and a second-brain memory system for an LLM agent, running daily and documented publicly. Previously: Lead Engineer at Opplane driving monolith-to-microservices migration and LLM-integration pipelines; Front-end Lead at Glartek shipping the core industrial-IoT product.",
                },
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                name: "Where is Gil Neto based and what languages does he speak?",
                acceptedAnswer: {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  text: "Based in Lisbon, Portugal. Native Portuguese, proficient English, elementary Spanish. Open to fractional and contract build work, across EU timezones.",
                },
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      })}
    />
    {import.meta.env.PROD && import.meta.env.PUBLIC_UMAMI_SCRIPT_URL && import.meta.env.PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID && (
      <script defer src={import.meta.env.PUBLIC_UMAMI_SCRIPT_URL} data-website-id={import.meta.env.PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID}></script>
    )}
  </head>
  <body class="antialiased">
    <slot />
  </body>
</html>
